# wikitui .desktop entry — packaging groundwork only.
#
# This file is NOT installed by `cargo install` or `cargo build`; it exists
# in-repo for distro packagers (nixpkgs/AUR/Debian/Fedora — PRD §8) to copy
# into their package's data files if they choose to.
#
# The MimeType line below declares wikitui as a handler for `wiki://` URIs
# per PRD FR-CS-7 ("Protocol handler: wiki:// x-scheme-handler via .desktop
# on Linux", v2/P2 — PRD.md §12, the "Scholar" milestone). `wikitui` itself
# now parses `wiki://`/`wiki:` URIs (`target::parse`, see that module's doc
# comment for the exact grammar): `Exec=wikitui %u` hands whatever URI a
# desktop environment dispatches straight through as the ordinary TITLE
# argument, which is all the CLI side of this feature needs. What this file
# does NOT do on its own is make the *desktop* route such URIs to wikitui in
# the first place — that is a one-time, per-machine registration step this
# file only declares support for, and it remains a packager/user action:
#
#   1. Install this file (or an equivalent) somewhere on the desktop's
#      `.desktop` search path, e.g. `~/.local/share/applications/` for a
#      per-user install, or the distro's usual system applications
#      directory for a packaged one.
#   2. Refresh the desktop database so it notices the new MimeType claim:
#        update-desktop-database ~/.local/share/applications
#   3. Register wikitui as the `wiki://` handler explicitly:
#        xdg-mime default wikitui.desktop x-scheme-handler/wiki
#      (`xdg-mime query default x-scheme-handler/wiki` confirms it stuck.)
#
# `Terminal=true` means the desktop environment opens a terminal emulator to
# run this — some desktops honor that per-.desktop-entry, others rely on a
# system-wide "run in terminal" default; if a `wiki://` link opens and
# immediately closes with nothing visible, that's the desktop's own
# terminal-launch behavior, not wikitui's — a packager targeting a specific
# desktop may need to wrap `Exec` in that desktop's preferred terminal
# invocation instead.
#
# macOS has no `.desktop`/`xdg-mime` equivalent; a `wiki://` handler there
# needs an app-bundle shim (a tiny `.app` wrapper registering the URL scheme
# via `CFBundleURLTypes` in its `Info.plist` and re-exec'ing this binary in
# `Terminal.app` or the user's preferred terminal). PRD FR-CS-7 marks that
# explicitly "best-effort" for v2 — it is documented here, not implemented;
# no such bundle ships in this repo.
[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=wikitui
GenericName=Wikipedia Reader
Comment=An unofficial, keyboard-first terminal client for Wikipedia (not endorsed by the Wikimedia Foundation)
Exec=wikitui %u
Terminal=true
Categories=Network;Utility;
MimeType=x-scheme-handler/wiki;
NoDisplay=false
